  lq:[["Why is there a lot of wet sand?","The tide is out.","It rained.","Someone washed it."],["What color is the bucket?","red","blue","green"],["How does the crab run?","sideways","backwards","very slowly"]],
  r:"Every shell on the beach was once the home of a small sea animal. When the animal grows, some of them, like the hermit crab, need to find a bigger shell to live in. That is why you should check that a shell is empty before you take it. Sand is also interesting. Much of it is made of tiny pieces of rock and broken shells that the waves have rubbed for thousands of years. So when you build a sandcastle, you are using very old material.",
