  r:"Coral reefs are like underwater cities. They look like rocks or plants, but corals are actually tiny animals that live together in huge groups. About a quarter of all sea creatures live on or near coral reefs. Fish use the reefs to hide from bigger hunters and to find food. Unfortunately, coral reefs are in danger because the seas are getting warmer. Divers and scientists are working hard to protect them.",
