  r:"A rocket needs a huge amount of power to escape the Earth's gravity. Most of a rocket is actually fuel. As the fuel burns, hot gas shoots out of the bottom and pushes the rocket up. Some modern rockets can land again after the launch, so they can be used many times. This makes space travel cheaper. Many countries, including Saudi Arabia and the United Arab Emirates, now have their own space programmes.",
