  r:"The International Space Station is the biggest object people have ever put into space. It is about as long as a football field and has been home to astronauts since the year two thousand. Fifteen countries worked together to build it, piece by piece. Inside, there are laboratories, a kitchen, a gym and small bedrooms. Life is not easy there, but the astronauts say that the view of the Earth makes everything worth it.",
