  r:"Animals move at very different speeds. A cheetah can run at more than one hundred kilometres an hour, but only for a short time. A camel is much slower, but it can walk for many hours without stopping. A garden snail is one of the slowest animals; it would need about a week to travel one kilometre. Faster is not always better. Each animal has the speed that it needs to survive in its home.",
